Task: Implement shared output module (src/gd_tools/output.py)

Summary:
Created src/gd_tools/output.py with shared rendering helpers for consistent
terminal output across all commands. The module provides:
- console: Shared Console instance (auto-detects terminal, no ANSI when piped)
- print_success(message): [OK] marker in green
- print_error(message): [FAIL] marker in red
- print_warning(message): yellow text
- print_info(message): cyan text
- print_summary(status, counts, files_checked, extra_info): summary footer with
  color coding (green=pass, red=fail, yellow=warning)
- print_table(table): wrapper around console.print(table)

Files created:
- src/gd_tools/output.py (shared output module)
- tests/unit/test_output.py (17 unit tests, 100% line/branch coverage)

Why: Establishes a unified visual language for all CLI commands per the
standardize terminal output spec (FR-1). Color semantics and markers follow
product-guidelines.md sections 2.1 and 7.
